# Firebase configuration
# Get these from your Firebase project settings → General → Your apps
#
# These are public by design — they only identify the project. Security
# comes from Firestore + Storage Rules and from API key restrictions in
# the GCP Console (HTTP referrer + API allowlist), NOT from keeping these
# values out of the bundle.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DO NOT add VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY (or any other Gemini/Maps/secret key) to
# this file. Anything VITE_* prefixed is bundled into the browser JS and
# is trivially extractable by anyone who loads the page. Sensitive keys
# live ONLY in Firebase Secret Manager and are consumed server-side.
#
# To set the server-side keys:
#   firebase functions:secrets:set GEMINI_API_KEY
#   firebase functions:secrets:set GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY
#
# The browser reaches Gemini via the broker callables
# (mintGeminiLiveToken, invokeGemini, embedGemini); Maps/Weather via
# geoProxy. See DEPLOYMENT.md for details.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
